tip: | Look at the boat. | A hull runs along the grid like a wall, but it comes to a point. Sails stand in the same plane as the hull, so they lean with it.
tip: 1 | Hull, mast, two triangles. | A boat is a very short list of shapes. Most of the work is in where they meet.
tip: 3 | Sails are lit too. | White cloth still has steps: lightest at the top where it faces the sky, a step down toward the boom.
tip: 4 | Water marks. | A few dashes on the tile say water. Too many and the boat stops being the subject.
